Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:03:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] NDCodeSimulator: the replay canonizer proved

Turing.exists_replayCanonizer: a primitive recursive list function rc_g keeps
the ND serialization's header and re-emits its two slice tables as the replay
machine's table (each record widened at the bit level by the choice tape's
field), compiled by codePrim_machine with a monotone running-maximum bound
and composed with the scheme's canonizer. The proof is the megafill C
review's (sealed over 21 definitions there); landed here with docstrings, a
proof sketch and an Implementation paragraph. The interpreter core and the
universal NDTM are now admission-free; the two status texts say so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
